{"id":"931966e7-5c1d-4f50-b4c0-114a088d6f3e","object":"chat.completion","created":1784813244,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    payload = case['payload']\\n    edges = payload['edges']\\n    refinement = payload['refinement']\\n    # Build membership: group -> sorted list of nodes\\n    membership = {}\\n    for node, group in refinement.items():\\n        membership.setdefault(group, []).append(node)\\n    for group in membership:\\n        membership[group].sort()\\n    # Sort groups by their identifier (string)\\n    sorted_groups = sorted(membership.keys())\\n    membership_lists = [membership[g] for g in sorted_groups]\\n    # Aggregate edges\\n    agg = {}\\n    for u, v, w in edges:\\n        gu = refinement[u]\\n        gv = refinement[v]\\n        if gu <= gv:\\n            key = (gu, gv)\\n        else:\\n            key = (gv, gu)\\n        agg[key] = agg.get(key, 0) + w\\n    # Convert to sorted list\\n    aggregate_edges = []\\n    for (g1, g2), total in sorted(agg.items()):\\n        aggregate_edges.append([g1, g2, total])\\n    return {'aggregate_edges': aggregate_edges, 'membership': membership_lists}\"}","reasoning_content":"We need to generate a Python function `solve(case)` that implements the described task. The case has edges (list of [v1, v2, weight]) and refinement (mapping from node to group). The task is to perform Leiden refinement and aggregation: map each node to a refined community (but note: input already has a refinement? Actually the input case has \"refinement\" field that maps nodes to groups. This is likely the initial partition? Or the refinement to be used? The description says \"parent-community constraints\" and \"refinement\" in the input. The task is to implement refinement and aggregation phases. The input \"refinement\" likely indicates the current partition of nodes into groups. Then we need to perform aggregation: constru